WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.920
- All right, time's
almost up on this hour,

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:04.260
but first I wanna share
one more uplifting story.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:05.093
This is What I'm Liking.

00:00:05.093 --> 00:00:08.055
(upbeat music)
(audience cheering)

00:00:08.055 --> 00:00:10.350
So, I've always been an outdoor girl.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:11.640
I grew up that way,

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:12.810
but the same can't be said

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:14.640
for lots of kids who
grew up in big cities.

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:15.930
That's why a Charlotte man is

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:19.530
taking dozens of kids in his
community under his wing,

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:21.900
teaching them the skills
and joys of camping,

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:23.310
which is so cool.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.050
From Camping with Cradle,

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:29.700
let's welcome Keith Cradle
watching on WCCB Charlotte CW.

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:32.610
What's up, man?
(audience cheering)

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:34.380
- Hey, Kelly, how are you doing?

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.490
- I am doing so well.

00:00:35.490 --> 00:00:37.440
So, why did you wanna do this?

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.150
- Well, I just love the outdoors,

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.620
and I know you do too,

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.060
but so many kids here in Charlotte

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.500
just don't have that opportunity

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.600
and so we created Camping with Cradle

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:47.790
to provide that outlet and an opportunity

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:50.370
to get them backpacking,
camping, and hiking.

00:00:50.370 --> 00:00:51.210
I previously worked

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:52.740
for the Mecklenburg
County Sheriff's Office

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:54.450
where I was director of youth programming,

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.460
and so I was working to
help rehabilitate kids,

00:00:56.460 --> 00:00:57.293
and the sheriff said,

00:00:57.293 --> 00:00:59.100
"Hey, what's one thing
that you'd love to do

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:00.120
that we haven't?"

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:01.530
It was Camping 101.

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:02.700
It grew from there.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.070
And to date, we've taken 60 kids out

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:06.420
camping and backpacking,

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.771
and really diversifying the outdoors,

00:01:07.771 --> 00:01:11.070
and letting them know that
they belong in those spaces.

00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:13.980
- Absolutely, it's so therapeutic as well

00:01:13.980 --> 00:01:15.660
just to get outdoors

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:17.790
and be, like, one with nature,

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:20.130
at the risk of sounding like a hippie,

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:21.240
but, like, it is.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:22.800
It's a beautiful thing
just to get outdoors

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:23.940
and outside of a city,

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:27.390
and just have quiet, and
be still, and enjoy nature.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:28.590
It's really cool what you're doing.

00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:30.884
So they're able to experience
this free of charge,

00:01:30.884 --> 00:01:32.545
which is the coolest part, right?

00:01:32.545 --> 00:01:34.440
- That's the whole reason why we do it.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:35.670
We want to bridge that gap

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:38.430
when it comes to access and
inclusion in the outdoors.

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:40.380
And so, all the outings are free,

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:42.330
and for kids that go backpacking with us,

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:43.920
they have an opportunity
to keep that gear,

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:46.950
so they don't have to go
out and pay for it later on.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:48.960
We teach them about outdoor safety,

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.130
of course, plant life,

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:50.963
but no matter what,

00:01:50.963 --> 00:01:53.220
they always seem to find the poison ivy.

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.470
And then they also get journals as well,

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.270
so they can document that experience,

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:59.280
and we talk about that around the fire.

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:00.960
And, once again, it's
just a great opportunity

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.160
for them to recreate

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:04.320
and not have those phones for a few days.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:06.900
- Absolutely, thank you so much, Keith.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.339
This is so cool, what you're doing.

00:02:08.339 --> 00:02:09.837
- Thank you.
- I'm liking your post

00:02:09.837 --> 00:02:10.893
right now, man.

00:02:10.893 --> 00:02:12.830
(audience cheering)
- [Keith] Thank you.

00:02:12.830 --> 00:02:13.980
- Well, that's not all.

00:02:13.980 --> 00:02:16.620
Our season-long partner,
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.300
the go-to pen of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:21.060
want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like you, sir.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.060
So they're gonna be writing
Camping with Cradle a check

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:25.260
for $1,000.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.093
How's that sound?

00:02:26.093 --> 00:02:28.500
(audience cheering)
- Oh, wow, thank you.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:29.700
- Absolutely, man.

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:30.533
Thank you so much,

00:02:30.533 --> 00:02:32.100
and thank you to all our guests this hour,

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.200
Ken Jeong, Charlie Day, Guy Branum,

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.090
Alex Cooper, and Corey.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.530
Y'all have a great day,

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.280
and if it's not, try and change it.

